On Fri, Jan 2, 2009 at 10:47 AM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Which family takes precedence if both are in a sentence?  FA or SE?
> eg.
> I talk to you about the book in lojban
> mi tavla do le cukta


SE does.  SE binds so closely that it's often folded into the same
word: se tavla --> selta'a

For some people I think it might be useful to look at a series of
sentences like the following, all of which have the same meaning.

.i mi tavla do le cukta la .lojban.
.i mi do tavla le cukta la .lojban.
.i mi do le cukta cu tavla la .lojban.
.i mi do le cukta la .lojban. tavla
.i do se tavla mi le cukta la .lojban.
.i do mi se tavla le cukta la .lojban.
.i do mi le cutka cu se tavla la .lojban.
.i do mi le cukta la .lojban. se tavla
.i le cukta cu te tavla do mi la .lojban.
.i le cukta do te tavla mi la .lojban.
.i le cukta do mi te tavla la .lojban.
.i le cukta do mi la .lojban. te tavla
.i la .lojban. ve tavla do le cukta mi
.i la .lojban. do ve tavla le cukta mi
.i la .lojban. do le cukta cu ve tavla mi
.i la .lojban. do le cukta mi ve tavla

also

.i fa mi fe do fi le cukta fo la .lojban. tavla
.i fe mi fa do fi le cukta fo la .lojban. se tavla
.i fi mi fe do fa le cukta fo la .lojban. te tavla
.i fo mi fe do fi le cukta fa la .lojban. ve tavla


The SE establishes a ground and then the sumti go in the slots.

One of the most important things you should learn about the official
rules about what happens if you use a FA tag and then next an
unlabelled sumti and things like that is-- DON"!T  Geez, it's crazy!
Once you've tagged one thing, you should keep tagging for the rest of
the sentence, because us mere mortals are just trying to read here.
Tricks like that (or the sevetevexeseteve shell game for instance) can
be fun puzzles but should be kept away from practical communication.

SE is really part of a bag of tricks (along with jai) for bringing
things to the x1, which is both convenient (when you say a sumti and
then want to say what it does, often it "te" or "ve" something) and
necessary (because the x1 is what gets used by gadri & etc).  FA is
part of a bag of tricks for conveniently tying things into a bridi,
along with BAI and tense tagging and so forth.  They are perfectly
safe when operated properly!

It even makes sense after a while. :)  I rarely look at a sentence
anymore and feel confused about its place structure.  At first "se"
seems like a transformation, but eventually it seems like.. well, like
the ordinary x2 is in the x1 slot and viceversa.  And like that makes
sense!  Promise.


